desc:K50 [workstation synth] (GFX Lab)
//tags: instrument synth workstation la fm epiano clav bells pad bass strings choir brass organ
//author: JGWizrad / Garden FX (GFX)
//
// Requires gfx-lab-drift, gfx-lab-output, gfx-lab-ui, gfx-lab-panel and gfx-lab-instrument (.jsfx-inc) in the same folder.
//
// K50: the successor to Lab80 (now archived), in the spirit of the late-80s linear-arithmetic workstations - a short
// struck or breathed attack over a synthesised body. Every sound is synthesised (no samples).
// STATUS: Lab copy of the Stable K50 v2.0 (deployed 30 Oct 2026: two voices, COMBIs, FX). Layout by JG, 30 Oct 2026.
// TWO VOICES: every note plays two of the 96 sounds, VOICE 1 (left half of the panel) and VOICE 2 (right half), each
//   with its own LEVEL (off, -48 .. +6 dB). MIX blends the two over the note (JG, 30 Oct 2026): in the centre both play
//   as their sounds were made (a layer); towards 1 voice 1 becomes the attack and voice 2 the body, towards 2 the other
//   way round. The attack voice plays in full for the first third of its length (set by the COMBI, 250 ms otherwise),
//   then falls smoothly to a lower level, and at the end of the dial to silence (the voice ends). (15 ms glides.)
//   Each voice: CUTOFF, RESO, TONE, TUNE (+/- 24 semitones: whole steps, Shift-drag for cents) and an AMP ENVELOPE - ATTACK, DECAY, RELEASE (x 0.25 - x 4 of the
//   sound's own times, centre = as made) and SUSTAIN (- 100 % = none, centre = the sound's own, + 100 % = full). A new
//   sound puts its voice's CUTOFF, RESO, TONE and AMP ENVELOPE back to the centre. Voice 1 carries the SPLITS'
//   left-hand part and the sound's own chorus / echo / tremolo; voice 2 has 8 voices of its own and always plays chords.
//   With voice 2's LEVEL off (the default) every sound plays as in the Stable.
// FX (both voices, after the sound's own chorus / echo, before the reverb): CHORUS (two delay lines swinging in
//   quadrature), PAN / TREM (an autopan or tremolo), DELAY (each repeat a little darker, ping-pong; DELAY SYNC: a note
//   value or free), REVERB (the GFX Space engine, a hall) - one amount dial each, 0 = off (a unit fades in / out, 15 ms).
//   A COMBI also sets each unit's rate / depth / feedback / mode, which have no dials.
// COMBIS (the COMBI bar at the top; the Combi parameter in REAPER's list): 16 combinations of both voices, their
//   blend, their controls and the FX: INIT, HAMMER STRINGS, PIZZ OVER PAD, GLASS CHOIR, CLAV BRASS, MALLET PAD,
//   BREATH STRINGS, BELL ORGAN, PLUCK ATMOSPHERE, TINE CELLO, HARP VOICES, MARIMBA BASS, STAB SECTION, WIDE KEYS,
//   TREMOLO EP, ECHO LEAD (each levelled to the house level by its own trim).
// ENGINES: analogue (two oscillators + sub into a 4-pole filter, with bell-partial, plucked-string, breath / chiff
//   and "aah" choir layers), 4-operator FM e-piano, plucked string (clav), struck metal bar, synthetic piano, organ
//   (drawbars, a cathedral principal chorus, a harmonium reed). One sound at a time; changing sound fades the old one
//   out (12 ms) and the new one in.
// SPLITS: the six SPLITS sounds play a second part with the left hand, below C4 (MIDI 60), on four voices of its own:
//   an upright, electric or slap bass (a plucked string over a sine body), the FM e-piano, or a log drum.
// SOUNDS (a click on a voice's display; its < > step through them in list order):
//   PIANOS & KEYS       - SESSION PIANO, BRIGHT PIANO, PIANO FIFTY, PIANISSIMO, SYNTHETIC ELECTRIC, PCM E-PIANO,
//                         CHORUS EP, FM E-PIANO, CLAV, HARPSICHORD STABS
//   ORGANS              - SLOW ROTOR, ROCK ORGAN, DRAWBAR ORGAN, CATHEDRAL ORGAN (the pipes speak and die away),
//                         SYN-HARMONIUM (two reeds beating)
//   MALLETS & BELLS     - FANTASIA, GAMELAN BELL, EASTERN BELLS, VIBRAPHONE (motor tremolo), BASS MARIMBA, SYN MARIMBA,
//                         TINE WAVE, METAL HARP, GLOCKENSPIEL, CRYSTAL HARP
//   GUITARS & PLUCKS    - LA NYLON, LA STEEL, LA CLEAN, LA HARMONICS, PICKED GUITAR, GRIITTTARR (driven), STEEL PICK, HARP,
//                         HOLLOWED HARP (a harp with a hollow, woody body)
//   PADS                - SOUNDTRACK, STACCATO HEAVEN, NYLON ATMOSPHERE, SPACIOUS SWEEP, AFTERTHOUGHT, FUTURE PAD,
//                         STEREO POLYSYNTH, SYNTH PAD, WARM PAD, DIGITAL NATIVE DANCE (a tempo-synced log-drum loop)
//   CHOIRS & VOICES     - GLASS VOICES, LA VOICES, CHOIR, O K CHORALE, DARK VOX, FANTASY VOX, SPACED VOX
//   STRINGS & ORCHESTRA - ARCO STRINGS, LEGATO STRINGS, COMBIE STRINGS, STRING ENSEMBLE, PRESSURE STRINGS (aftertouch
//                         opens, swells and adds vibrato), JETE STRINGS, STRINGS, FAT STRINGS, DIGITAL CELLO,
//                         HORNS & STRINGS, PIZZAGOGO
//   BRASS               - HORN SECTION, RICH BRASS, VELO-BRASS, SLAP BRASS, FLUTISH BRASS, BONES (slides), SYNTH BRASS,
//                         VELO STAB
//   LEADS & FLUTES      - LIVING CALLIOPE, BREATHY CHIFFER, PIPE SOLO, SHAKUHACHI, BOTTLE BLOWER, SHAMUS THEME,
//                         PAN FLUTE, SQUARE LEAD, HOOVER (most leads are mono with glide)
//   BASSES              - SYNTH BASS, ANALOGUE BASS, SUB, ACID, ROUND, PLUCK, HOLLOW, REESE (mono with glide)
//   FX                  - NIGHTMARE, INTRUDER FX, ORCHESTRA HIT
//   SPLITS              - JAZZ GUITAR DUO, FLUTE-PIANO DUO, BASIN BLUES, CIRCLE SESSION, E-BASS AND E-PIANO,
//                         SLAP BASS N BRASS
// Levels: every sound is matched to its kind (pads / strings / bells about -21.5 dB RMS on a test phrase, keys -21 to
//   -22, organs and leads -20, basses -17); eight notes at full velocity stay inside the output stage's ceiling.
// DRIFT (0 - 100 %, 50 % = standard): fine tuning and the attack (JG, 29 Oct 2026). Tuning: a slow pitch wander
//   and each note a little out (every engine). Attack: each note's attack transient (hammer, mallet, chiff, tine bark,
//   bell partials) a little different (+/- 30 %); each note's attack length a little longer or shorter (+/- 25 %) and its
//   attack louder or softer (+/- 20 %), and voice 2 a few cents off voice 1 (+/- 8). No filter or chorus drift.
// MIDI: notes, sustain (CC64), mod wheel (CC1, vibrato), channel / poly aftertouch (the sounds made for it open
//   their filter, swell or add vibrato as you press), all-notes-off (CC120 / 123); released on transport stop.
// GUI (1080 x 820, one page): the COMBI bar; the ATTACK BLEND strip (voice 1's sound, LEVEL | MIX between two glowing circles |
//   voice 2's, mirrored); VOICE 1 and VOICE 2 side by side (FILTER & TUNE, AMP ENVELOPE); FX; DRIFT / MIDI / MASTER.
//   A voice whose LEVEL is off is greyed.

import gfx-lab-drift.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-output.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-ui.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-panel.jsfx-inc
import gfx-lab-instrument.jsfx-inc

slider1:0<0,95,1{Fm E-Piano,Clav,Glockenspiel,Synth Pad,Warm Pad,Analogue Bass,Strings,String Ensemble,Fantasia,Staccato Heaven,Pizzagogo,Glass Voices,Nylon Atmosphere,Synth Brass,Crystal Harp,Sub Bass,Acid Bass,Round Bass,Pluck Bass,Hollow Bass,Reese Bass,Digital Native Dance,Living Calliope,Soundtrack,Session Piano,Chorus Ep,Dark Vox,Fantasy Vox,Spaced Vox,Velo Stab,Hoover,Fat Strings,Orchestra Hit,Horn Section,Drawbar Organ,Pan Flute,Harp,Square Lead,Bright Piano,La Nylon,La Steel,La Clean,La Harmonics,Arco Strings,Combie Strings,Pressure Strings,Jete Strings,Legato Strings,Digital Cello,Horns & Strings,Spacious Sweep,Afterthought,Future Pad,Stereo Polysynth,La Voices,Choir,O K Chorale,Metal Harp,Bass Marimba,Gamelan Bell,Vibraphone,Eastern Bells,Syn Marimba,Tine Wave,Synthetic Electric,Pcm E-Piano,Piano Fifty,Pianissimo,Harpsichord Stabs,Slow Rotor,Rock Organ,Cathedral Organ,Syn-Harmonium,Griitttarr,Breathy Chiffer,Slap Brass,Rich Brass,Pipe Solo,Shamus Theme,Flutish Brass,Hollowed Harp,Shakuhachi,Picked Guitar,Nightmare,Velo-Brass,Intruder Fx,Steel Pick,Synth Bass,Bones,Bottle Blower,Jazz Guitar Duo,Flute-Piano Duo,Basin Blues,Circle Session,E-Bass And E-Piano,Slap Bass N Brass}>-Voice 1 sound
